# Plugin Integration Guide

Purpose:
  How SDDRA adapts external plugins and integrates them into the chain graph.

External Source:
  D:\Tasks\ai_code\vkard.az\tmp\external-repo-audit\repo-01
  Upstream: https://github.com/obra/superpowers

Adaptation Rules:
  1. Only general-purpose skills are adapted
  2. Domain-specific skills are rejected
  3. External dependencies are not added
  4. Adapted skills MUST fit SDDRA token budget
  5. Adapted skills MUST respect human gates

Adapted Plugins:
  brainstorming -> P1 arm
  test-driven-development -> QA chain (TS stage)
  systematic-debugging -> Bugfix/Hotfix chains (AR stage)
  writing-plans -> S1 arm
  using-git-worktrees -> C1 arm
  code-review -> R1 arm
  verification-before-completion -> R1 arm
  dispatching-parallel-agents -> Scheduler
  writing-skills -> Skill creation

Rejected Plugins:
  executing-plans: superseded by chain graph
  finishing-a-development-branch: project-specific
  subagent-driven-development: covered by chain graph
  using-superpowers: meta-skill, not needed
  visual-companion: UI-specific
  condition-based-waiting: too specific
  defense-in-depth: covered by security rules
  spec-document-reviewer-prompt: domain-specific

Integration Points:
  .sdd/chains/arms/prompt.sdd -> brainstorming
  .sdd/chains/arms/sdd.sdd -> writing-plans
  .sdd/chains/arms/code.sdd -> using-git-worktrees
  .sdd/chains/arms/review.sdd -> code-review, verification-before-completion
  .sdd/chains/feature.sdd -> test-driven-development, dispatching-parallel-agents
  .sdd/chains/bugfix.sdd -> systematic-debugging
  .sdd/chains/hotfix.sdd -> systematic-debugging

Usage:
  Plugins are referenced by chain arms in their skills section.
  AI loads plugin adapters only when entering the relevant stage.
  No plugin code is executed outside its designated stage.

Token Impact:
  Each plugin adapter adds ~500-2000 tokens to its stage.
  Total plugin overhead: ~10,000 tokens across full workflow.
   Within 70,000 token budget.

State: +
